# What Vercel may upload (#677). ALLOWLIST — deny everything, then re-admit
# only the client build's inputs.
#
# The CLI does not read `.gitignore`, so without this file `vercel deploy`
# walks the whole checkout: `node_modules/` (731 MB) plus `.claude/`, the agent
# worktrees and their own `node_modules/` (44 GB). The first manual mirror
# deploy failed on it — "`files` should NOT have more than 15000 items,
# received 48318".
#
# It is an allowlist rather than a list of exclusions ON PURPOSE (Codex P1/P2
# on #677). A denylist uploads whatever it forgot to name, and the things it
# forgets are exactly the dangerous ones: gitignored local secrets that the
# clean-worktree guard cannot see because git does not track them
# (`serviceAccountKey.json`, `.env.local`), plus every future build artifact
# (`coverage/`, `playwright-report/`, `test-results/`, `.venv/`, `dist/`).
# Denying by default makes a new secret or artifact excluded until someone
# deliberately admits it.
#
# The build runs `npm run build` (Vite) on Vercel and installs its own
# dependencies, so this is the complete set of inputs. Adding a root-level
# build input means adding a `!` line here, and the deploy will fail loudly
# if you forget rather than shipping something wrong. app-ci also builds the
# tracked admission set in an empty directory to catch missing inputs on PRs
# (#1674); that local compile does not verify Vercel upload traversal.

# Deny everything at the repo root, recursively.
/*

# Re-admit the client build's inputs, and nothing else.
!/index.html
!/package.json
!/package-lock.json
!/vite.config.ts
!/tsconfig.json
!/tsconfig.sw.json
!/vercel.json
!/src
!/public

# One server-side module the client build imports (`src/data/hostnames.ts`,
# #1655): the shared public-projection field list. Admit exactly that file —
# `functions/` also holds the gitignored per-project `.env.*` files, so the
# directory itself stays denied. Each parent is re-admitted and then emptied
# again, because an ignored directory's children cannot be re-included.
!/functions
/functions/*
!/functions/src
/functions/src/*
!/functions/src/publicHostnameFields.ts
